WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.547
Every video starts as an idea.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.297
What if that idea was a template?

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.544
LeClap. One template. Every screen.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.940
Describe your video once, as a template. LeClap turns it into a finished film.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.484
The same template works on your computer, in your browser, and right on your phone.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:31.635
On desktop: pick a template. Drop in your footage. Trim the best take. Build your scenes, right in the browser.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.607
But here's the magic.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.643
Pick a template. Shoot your clip.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.339
And the phone renders the video itself.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.000
No server. No upload. It all stays on the device.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:53.194
Social stories. Brand intros. Product demos. Personalised videos.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.758
And for agentic development: your coding agent records the change, and LeClap renders the proof.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.620
Before: a faint link, and no feedback.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.473
After: one button, and the cart opens.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.313
Don't describe the change. Show it.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.494
LeClap. One template. Every screen.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.588
Open source, at leclap.dev.
